4. **Default Stabilization Movement**: When all other conditions are met (velocity and angle within limits), choose a default direction (e.g., right) to maintain balance without overcorrecting, preventing unnecessary oscillations while ensuring stability.

By following these steps, you can effectively balance the pole with minimal corrections, reducing the risk of destabilization.
